provenance], which is undefined behavior to dereference. To properly\nrestore the lost information and obtain a dereferenceable pointer, use\n[`with_addr`][pointer::with_addr] or [`map_addr`][pointer::map_addr].\n\nIf using those APIs is not possible because there is no way to preserve a pointer with the\nrequired provenance, then Strict Provenance might not be for you. Use pointer-integer casts\nor [`expose_provenance`][pointer::expose_provenance] and [`with_exposed_provenance`][with_exposed_provenance]\ninstead. However, note that this makes your code less portable and less amenable to tools\nthat check for compliance with the Rust memory model.\n\nOn most platforms this will produce a value with the same bytes as the original\npointer, because all the bytes are dedicated to describing the address.\nPlatforms which need to store additional information in the pointer may\nperform a change of representation to produce a value containing only the address\nportion of the pointer. What that means is up to the platform to define.\n\nThis is a [Strict Provenance][crate::ptr#strict-provenance] API.\n"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [without_provenance]: without_provenance_mut"}],"inline":"Always","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":216}],"output":{"Deduplicated":218}},"src":"TopLevel","is_global_initializer":null,"body":"Opaque"},{"def_id":2,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["ptr",0]},{"Ident":["with_exposed_provenance_mut",0]},{"Instantiated":{"params":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":214}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"kind":"Other"}}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":2,"beg":{"line":1045,"col":0},"end":{"line":1045,"col":66}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Converts an address back to a mutable pointer, picking up some previously 'exposed'"},{"DocComment":" [provenance][crate::ptr#provenance]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This is fully equivalent to `addr as *mut T`. The provenance of the returned pointer is that"},{"DocComment":" of *some* pointer that was previously exposed by passing it to"},{"DocComment":" [`expose_provenance`][pointer::expose_provenance], or a `ptr as usize` cast. In addition, memory"},{"DocComment":" which is outside the control of the Rust abstract machine (MMIO registers, for example) is"},{"DocComment":" always considered to be accessible with an exposed provenance, so long as this memory is disjoint"},{"DocComment":" from memory that will be used by the abstract machine such as the stack, heap, and statics."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The exact provenance that gets picked is not specified. The compiler will do its best to pick"},{"DocComment":" the \"right\" provenance for you (whatever that may be), but currently we cannot provide any"},{"DocComment":" guarantees about which provenance the resulting pointer will have -- and therefore there"},{"DocComment":" is no definite specification for which memory the resulting pointer may access."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If there is *no* previously 'exposed' provenance that justifies the way the returned pointer"},{"DocComment":" will be used, the program has undefined behavior. In particular, the aliasing rules still apply:"},{"DocComment":" pointers and references that have been invalidated due to aliasing accesses cannot be used"},{"DocComment":" anymore, even if they have been exposed!"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Due to its inherent ambiguity, this operation may not be supported by tools that help you to"},{"DocComment":" stay conformant with the Rust memory model. It is recommended to use [Strict"},{"DocComment":" Provenance][self#strict-provenance] APIs such as [`with_addr`][pointer::with_addr] wherever"},{"DocComment":" possible."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" On most platforms this will produce a value with the same bytes as the address. Platforms"},{"DocComment":" which need to store additional information in a pointer may not support this operation,"},{"DocComment":" since it is generally not possible to actually *compute* which provenance the returned"},{"DocComment":" pointer has to pick up."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This is an [Exposed Provenance][crate::ptr#exposed-provenance] API."},{"Builtin":{"TrackCaller":{"data":{"file_id":2,"beg":{"line":1043,"col":17},"end":{"line":1043,"col":29}},"generated_from_span":null}}}],"inline":"Always","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":218}],"output":{"Deduplicated":216}},"src":"TopLevel","is_global_initializer":null,"body":"Opaque"}],"global_decls":[],"trait_decls":[],"trait_impls":[],"ordered_decls":[{"Fun":{"NonRec":2}},{"Fun":{"NonRec":1}},{"Fun":{"NonRec":0}}]},"has_errors":false}